Mutation evidence
Six meaningful fixture-copy mutations killed: entry suppression, terminal-output suppression, restored rollback/disarm/error machinery, held budget accounting, unsanitized held budget, post-output alarm deletion.
No productive mutation survived; every copied mutant was restored, production was never mutated.
An exploratory forged preliminary COUNT survived because the unchanged locked persisted-count verification independently rejects missing/malformed budgets; it is equivalent on that scenario and was replaced with an unsanitized-count mutation that the regression kills.
An initial overly broad rollback mutation broke the nested reproduction setup and was not counted; the final mutation restores the full prior rollback/disarm behavior and fails specifically on replacement alarm deletion.

Scope and artifacts
All fakes and operational state used new temporary fixture homes; no real home mutation or real-time waits were added.
No property/model suite exists for this behavior; existing deterministic sequences were extended.
Full suite, pipeline, live-harness integration, startup, fleet mutations, status append, nested agents, branch changes, commit, remote operations and review were not run.
Result and settled-decision handoff: captain-hold-fix-3-result.md and captain-hold-fix-3-handoff.md in the branch directory.
Detailed red/green, original reproduction, mutation and check receipts: adv-review-loop/captain-hold-fix-3-evidence under this worktree's git directory.

